# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NexMeet client environment
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Local dev ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to the Vite origin, which proxies /api and /socket.io to the
# backend (see vite.config.ts) — so usually NOTHING needs to be set.

# ── Split-origin production deployment (Vercel frontend + EC2 backend) ──
# Set these in your Vercel Project Settings (Environment Variables).
# All three are required on Vercel:
#
# Backend REST API (AWS EC2 instance URL):
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
#
# Socket.IO chat/presence (AWS EC2 instance, wss://):
# VITE_SOCKET_URL=wss://api.yourdomain.com
#
# LiveKit signaling (AWS EC2 SFU instance behind Caddy TLS):
# VITE_LIVEKIT_WS_URL=wss://sfu.yourdomain.com
#
# NOTE: VITE_* variables are baked into the bundle at BUILD time on Vercel.
# Updating environment variables in Vercel triggers a rebuild automatically.
